IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa14-nouns`

-- coa14-ch09-classes.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 17 Chapter 9 "Classes of share and class rights", ss 629 to 640 (lines 8437-8526).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone. How to read an answer: see coa14-ch07-premiums.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE with
-- a FALSE-kind comment, NOTHING with a NOTHING-kind comment). A function titled as a bar answers JUST TRUE where the text says no
-- to the act, JUST FALSE where the bar does not apply, NOTHING where the text does not decide.
-- SEAMS: facts another part answers are inputs named for the answering section (s 283, s 1121, s 18 ...).

§ `Chapter 9 -- Classes of share and class rights`

§§ `s 629 Classes of shares`

-- src:8440 | (1) For the purposes of the Companies Acts shares are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform.
@ref s 629(1) Classes of shares (src:8440)
GIVEN `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629(1) the shares are of one class` MEANS
    IF `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform"

-- src:8441 | (2) For this purpose the rights attached to shares are not regarded as different from those attached to other shares by reason only that they do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment.
@ref s 629(2) Classes of shares: the dividend difference (src:8441)
GIVEN `the only reason the rights differ is that the shares do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629(2) the rights attached to the shares are regarded as different` MEANS
    IF `the only reason the rights differ is that the shares do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the rights attached to shares are not regarded as different from those attached to other shares by reason only that they do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason only that": any other reason is for subsection (1)

-- The two together: the name PLAN.md section 4.2 gives the seam that other parts take as an input.
-- src:8440 | (1) For the purposes of the Companies Acts shares are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform.
-- src:8441 | (2) For this purpose the rights attached to shares are not regarded as different from those attached to other shares by reason only that they do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment.
@ref s 629(1) and (2) Classes of shares: whether shares are of the same class (src:8440-8441)
GIVEN `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the only reason the rights differ is that the shares do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 629 the shares are of the same class` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 629(1) the shares are of one class` `the rights attached to the shares are in all respects uniform` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 629(2) the rights attached to the shares are regarded as different` `the only reason the rights differ is that the shares do not carry the same rights to dividends in the twelve months immediately following their allotment` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST TRUE -- the dividend difference is disregarded, so the rights are not regarded as different
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shares are of one class if the rights attached to them are in all respects uniform"

§§ `s 630 Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital`

-- Lead-in, s 630(1): "This section is concerned with the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares in a company having a share capital"
-- (a scope statement: inert, fork F-signpost).

-- src:8445 | (2) Rights attached to a class of a company's shares may only be varied—
-- src:8446 | (a) in accordance with provision in the company's articles for the variation of those rights, or
-- src:8447 | (b) where the company's articles contain no such provision, if the holders of shares of that class consent to the variation in accordance with this section.
@ref s 630(2) Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital: the ways (src:8445-8447)
GIVEN `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 630(4) the consent required is given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630(2) the rights attached to the class may be varied in this way` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights`
    THEN IF `the variation is made in accordance with that provision`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights attached to a class of a company's shares may only be varied— (a) in accordance with provision in the company's articles for the variation of those rights"
    ELSE `s 630(4) the consent required is given` -- JUST FALSE is the text's no: "(b) where the company's articles contain no such provision, if the holders of shares of that class consent to the variation in accordance with this section"

-- src:8448 | (3) This is without prejudice to any other restrictions on the variation of the rights.
@ref s 630(3) Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital: other restrictions (src:8448)
GIVEN `another restriction on the variation of the rights applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630(3) the variation is subject to another restriction` MEANS
    IF `another restriction on the variation of the rights applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "This is without prejudice to any other restrictions" says nothing where there are none

-- src:8449 | (4) The consent required for the purposes of this section on the part of the holders of a class of a company's shares is—
-- src:8450 | (a) consent in writing from the holders of at least three-quarters in nominal value of the issued shares of that class (excluding any shares held as treasury shares), or
-- src:8451 | (b) a special resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class sanctioning the variation.
@ref s 630(4) Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital: the consent (src:8449-8451)
GIVEN `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` IS A NUMBER
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630(4) the consent required is given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF counted GREATER THAN 0 AND `the nominal value of the shares whose holders consented in writing` TIMES 4 AT LEAST 3 TIMES counted
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` AND `the resolution sanctions the variation` AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class` AND `the resolution sanctions the variation` AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283 (coa7)
        IF counted AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): with no issued shares outside treasury there is no nominal value to take three-quarters of
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The consent required ... is— (a) consent in writing from the holders of at least three-quarters in nominal value of the issued shares of that class (excluding any shares held as treasury shares), or (b) a special resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the holders of that class sanctioning the variation"
    WHERE
        counted MEANS `the nominal value of the issued shares of the class` MINUS `the nominal value of those shares held as treasury shares`

-- src:8452 | (5) Any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles, is itself to be treated as a variation of those rights.
@ref s 630(5) Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital: amending the articles (src:8452)
GIVEN `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630(5) the change is treated as a variation of those rights` MEANS
    IF `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares` OR `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the amendment of such a provision and the insertion of such a provision

-- src:8453 | (6) In this section, and (except where the context otherwise requires) in any provision in a company's articles for the variation of the rights attached to a class of shares, references to the variation of those rights include references to their abrogation.
@ref s 630(6) Variation of class rights: companies having a share capital: abrogation (src:8453)
GIVEN `the act is a variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the abrogation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 630(6) the act counts as a variation of the rights` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is a variation of the rights` OR `the act is the abrogation of the rights`
        THEN IF `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` AND `the context otherwise requires`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except where the context otherwise requires) in any provision in a company's articles"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include references to their abrogation" extends the term and says nothing of other acts

§§ `s 631 Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital`

-- Lead-in, s 631(1): "This section is concerned with the variation of the rights of a class of members of a company where the company does not have a share capital"
-- (a scope statement: inert, fork F-signpost).

-- src:8456 | (2) Rights of a class of members may only be varied—
-- src:8457 | (a) in accordance with provision in the company's articles for the variation of those rights, or
-- src:8458 | (b) where the company's articles contain no such provision, if the members of that class consent to the variation in accordance with this section.
@ref s 631(2) Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital: the ways (src:8456-8458)
GIVEN `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the variation is made in accordance with that provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 631(4) the consent required is given` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(2) the rights of the class of members may be varied in this way` MEANS
    IF `the articles contain provision for the variation of those rights`
    THEN IF `the variation is made in accordance with that provision`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Rights of a class of members may only be varied— (a) in accordance with provision in the company's articles for the variation of those rights"
    ELSE `s 631(4) the consent required is given` -- JUST FALSE is the text's no: "(b) where the company's articles contain no such provision, if the members of that class consent to the variation in accordance with this section"

-- src:8459 | (3) This is without prejudice to any other restrictions on the variation of the rights.
@ref s 631(3) Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital: other restrictions (src:8459)
GIVEN `another restriction on the variation of the rights applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(3) the variation is subject to another restriction` MEANS
    IF `another restriction on the variation of the rights applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "This is without prejudice to any other restrictions" says nothing where there are none

-- Note the difference from s 630(4)(a): there it is three-quarters IN NOMINAL VALUE of the issued shares; here it is three-quarters
-- OF THE MEMBERS of the class (counted by number).
-- src:8460 | (4) The consent required for the purposes of this section on the part of the members of a class is—
-- src:8461 | (a) consent in writing from at least three-quarters of the members of the class, or
-- src:8462 | (b) a special resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class sanctioning the variation.
@ref s 631(4) Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital: the consent (src:8460-8462)
GIVEN `the number of members of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who consented in writing` IS A NUMBER
      `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution sanctions the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(4) the consent required is given` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of members of the class` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of those members who consented in writing` TIMES 4 AT LEAST 3 TIMES `the number of members of the class`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` AND `the resolution sanctions the variation` AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the resolution was passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class` AND `the resolution sanctions the variation` AND `s 283 the resolution is a special resolution` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the resolution is a special resolution is s 283 (coa7)
        IF `the number of members of the class` AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a class with no members has no three-quarters
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The consent required ... is— (a) consent in writing from at least three-quarters of the members of the class, or (b) a special resolution passed at a separate general meeting of the members of that class sanctioning the variation"

-- src:8463 | (5) Any amendment of a provision contained in a company's articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members, or the insertion of any such provision into the articles, is itself to be treated as a variation of those rights.
@ref s 631(5) Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital: amending the articles (src:8463)
GIVEN `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(5) the change is treated as a variation of those rights` MEANS
    IF `the change is an amendment of a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members` OR `the change is the insertion of such a provision into the articles`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the amendment of such a provision and the insertion of such a provision

-- src:8464 | (6) In this section, and (except where the context otherwise requires) in any provision in a company's articles for the variation of the rights of a class of members, references to the variation of those rights include references to their abrogation.
@ref s 631(6) Variation of class rights: companies without a share capital: abrogation (src:8464)
GIVEN `the act is a variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the abrogation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context otherwise requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 631(6) the act counts as a variation of the rights` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the act is a variation of the rights` OR `the act is the abrogation of the rights`
        THEN IF `the reference is in a provision in the articles for the variation of the rights` AND `the context otherwise requires`
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except where the context otherwise requires) in any provision in a company's articles"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include references to their abrogation" extends the term and says nothing of other acts

§§ `s 632 Variation of class rights: saving for court's powers under other provisions`

-- src:8466 | Nothing in section 630 or 631 (variation of class rights) affects the power of the court under—
-- src:8467 | section 98 (application to cancel resolution for public company to be re-registered as private),
-- src:8468 | Part 26 (arrangements and reconstructions: general)
-- src:8469 | Part 26A (arrangements and reconstructions: companies in financial difficulty), or
-- src:8470 | Part 30 (protection of members against unfair prejudice).
@ref s 632 Variation of class rights: saving for court's powers under other provisions (src:8466-8470)
GIVEN power IS A `s 632 power of the court`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 632 section 630 or 631 affects the power of the court` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `s 632 the power of the court under section 98` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 630 or 631 (variation of class rights) affects the power of the court under— section 98"
    WHEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 630 or 631 ... affects the power of the court under— ... Part 26"
    WHEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 26A` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 630 or 631 ... affects the power of the court under— ... Part 26A"
    WHEN `s 632 the power of the court under Part 30` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in section 630 or 631 ... affects the power of the court under— ... Part 30"
    WHEN `s 632 some other power of the court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the saving names four powers and does not say whether sections 630 and 631 affect any other

§§ `s 633 Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital`

-- src:8472 | (1) This section applies where the rights attached to any class of shares in a company are varied under section 630 (variation of class rights: companies having a share capital).
@ref s 633(1) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: when it applies (src:8472)
GIVEN `the rights attached to a class of shares in the company are varied under section 630` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 633(1) section 633 applies` MEANS
    IF `the rights attached to a class of shares in the company are varied under section 630`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the rights attached to any class of shares in a company are varied under section 630" ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:8473 | (2) The holders of not less in the aggregate than 15% of the issued shares of the class in question (being persons who did not consent to or vote in favour of the resolution for the variation) may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled.
-- src:8474 | For this purpose any of the company's share capital held as treasury shares is disregarded.
@ref s 633(2) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: who may apply (src:8473-8474)
GIVEN `s 633(1) section 633 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of the issued shares of the class` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares that the company holds as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of shares held by the applicants` IS A NUMBER
      `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 633(2) the holders may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 633(1) section 633 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the rights attached to any class of shares in a company are varied under section 630"
        IF `s 633(1) section 633 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the rights were varied under section 630 is not known
        IF NOT `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of holders "being persons who did not consent to or vote in favour of the resolution for the variation"
        IF counted AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): with no issued shares outside treasury there is no 15% to take
        IF `the number of shares held by the applicants` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 15 TIMES counted
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "The holders of not less in the aggregate than 15% of the issued shares of the class in question"
    WHERE
        counted MEANS `the number of the issued shares of the class` MINUS `the number of those shares that the company holds as treasury shares`

-- src:8475 | (3) If such an application is made, the variation has no effect unless and until it is confirmed by the court.
@ref s 633(3) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: no effect until confirmed (src:8475)
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has confirmed the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 633(3) the variation is without effect unless and until the court confirms it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an application has been made`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such an application is made, the variation has no effect" (no application has been made)
        IF `the court has confirmed the variation`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless and until it is confirmed by the court" (the until is met)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8477 | (a) must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be), and
@ref s 633(4)(a) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: within 21 days (src:8477)
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 633(4)(a) the last day for the application` MEANS `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` PLUS 21

-- src:8477 | (a) must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be), and
@ref s 633(4)(a) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: in time (src:8477)
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 633(4)(a) the application was made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the application was made` LESS THAN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed"
        IF `the date the application was made` AT MOST `s 633(4)(a) the last day for the application` `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Application to the court (a) must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be)"

-- src:8478 | (b) may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose.
@ref s 633(4)(b) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: on behalf of the shareholders (src:8478)
GIVEN `the application is made by one or more of the shareholders entitled to make it on behalf of them all` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those making it were appointed by the shareholders in writing for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 633(4)(b) the application may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by one or more of the shareholders entitled to make it on behalf of them all` AND `those making it were appointed by the shareholders in writing for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made on behalf of the shareholders entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose"

-- src:8479 | (5) The court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons who apply to the court to be heard and appear to the court to be interested in the application, may, if satisfied having regard to all the circumstances of the case that the variation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant, disallow the variation, and shall if not so satisfied confirm it.
@ref s 633(5) Right to object to variation: companies having a share capital: the court confirms (src:8479)
