`s 633(5) the court shall confirm the variation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, that the variation would unfairly prejudice the shareholders of the class represented by the applicant`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court "may" disallow the variation where satisfied; the text does not say it must
