§§ `s 634 Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital`

-- src:8483 | (1) This section applies where the rights of any class of members of a company are varied under section 631 (variation of class rights: companies without a share capital).
@ref s 634(1) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: when it applies (src:8483)
GIVEN `the rights of a class of members of the company are varied under section 631` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(1) section 634 applies` MEANS
    IF `the rights of a class of members of the company are varied under section 631`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the rights of any class of members of a company are varied under section 631" ("where": ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- src:8484 | (2) Members amounting to not less than 15% of the members of the class in question (being persons who did not consent to or vote in favour of the resolution for the variation) may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled.
@ref s 634(2) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: who may apply (src:8484)
GIVEN `s 634(1) section 634 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the number of members of the class in question` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of members applying` IS A NUMBER
      `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(2) the members may apply to the court to have the variation cancelled` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 634(1) section 634 applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where the rights of any class of members of a company are varied under section 631"
        IF `s 634(1) section 634 applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the rights were varied under section 631 is not known
        IF NOT `none of the applicants consented to or voted in favour of the resolution for the variation`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of members "being persons who did not consent to or vote in favour of the resolution for the variation"
        IF `the number of members of the class in question` AT MOST 0
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a class with no members has no 15%
        IF `the number of members applying` TIMES 100 AT LEAST 15 TIMES `the number of members of the class in question`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is that of "Members amounting to not less than 15% of the members of the class in question"

-- src:8485 | (3) If such an application is made, the variation has no effect unless and until it is confirmed by the court.
@ref s 634(3) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: no effect until confirmed (src:8485)
GIVEN `an application has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has confirmed the variation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(3) the variation is without effect unless and until the court confirms it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `an application has been made`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If such an application is made, the variation has no effect" (no application has been made)
        IF `the court has confirmed the variation`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless and until it is confirmed by the court" (the until is met)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:8486 | (4) Application to the court must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be) and may be made on behalf of the members entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose.
@ref s 634(4) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: within 21 days (src:8486)
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 634(4) the last day for the application` MEANS `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` PLUS 21

-- src:8486 | (4) Application to the court must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be) and may be made on behalf of the members entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose.
@ref s 634(4) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: in time (src:8486)
GIVEN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(4) the application was made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date the application was made` LESS THAN `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed"
        IF `the date the application was made` AT MOST `s 634(4) the last day for the application` `the date the consent was given or the resolution was passed`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Application to the court must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be)"

-- src:8486 | (4) Application to the court must be made within 21 days after the date on which the consent was given or the resolution was passed (as the case may be) and may be made on behalf of the members entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose.
@ref s 634(4) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: on behalf of the members (src:8486)
GIVEN `the application is made by one or more of the members entitled to make it on behalf of them all` IS A BOOLEAN
      `those making it were appointed by the members in writing for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(4) the application may be made on behalf of the members entitled` MEANS
    IF `the application is made by one or more of the members entitled to make it on behalf of them all` AND `those making it were appointed by the members in writing for the purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be made on behalf of the members entitled to make the application by such one or more of their number as they may appoint in writing for the purpose"

-- src:8487 | (5) The court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons who apply to the court to be heard and appear to the court to be interested in the application, may, if satisfied having regard to all the circumstances of the case that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant, disallow the variation, and shall if not so satisfied confirm it.
@ref s 634(5) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: the court confirms (src:8487)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(5) the court shall confirm the variation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court "may" disallow the variation where satisfied; the text does not say it must
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:8487 | (5) The court, after hearing the applicant and any other persons who apply to the court to be heard and appear to the court to be interested in the application, may, if satisfied having regard to all the circumstances of the case that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant, disallow the variation, and shall if not so satisfied confirm it.
@ref s 634(5) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: the court disallows (src:8487)
GIVEN `the court is satisfied, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(5) the court may disallow the variation` MEANS
    IF `the court is satisfied, having regard to all the circumstances of the case, that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, if satisfied having regard to all the circumstances of the case that the variation would unfairly prejudice the members of the class represented by the applicant, disallow the variation"

-- src:8488 | The decision of the court on any such application is final.
@ref s 634(5) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: the decision is final (src:8488)
GIVEN `it is the decision of the court on an application under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(5) the decision of the court is final` MEANS
    IF `it is the decision of the court on an application under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The decision of the court on any such application is final"

-- src:8489 | (6) References in this section to the variation of the rights of a class of members include references to their abrogation.
@ref s 634(6) Right to object to variation: companies without a share capital: abrogation (src:8489)
GIVEN `the act is a variation of the rights of a class of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the act is the abrogation of those rights` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 634(6) the act counts as a variation of the rights of a class of members` MEANS
    IF `the act is a variation of the rights of a class of members` OR `the act is the abrogation of those rights`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include references to their abrogation" extends the term and says nothing of other acts

§§ `s 635 Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar`

-- src:8491 | (1) The company must within 15 days after the making of an order by the court on an application under section 633 or 634 (objection to variation of class rights) forward a copy of the order to the registrar.
@ref s 635(1) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar (src:8491)
GIVEN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 635(1) the last day for the copy of the order` MEANS `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` PLUS 15

GIVEN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 635(1) the number of days allowed for the copy of the order` MEANS
    (Day (`s 635(1) the last day for the copy of the order` `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`)) MINUS (Day `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`)

-- src:8491 | (1) The company must within 15 days after the making of an order by the court on an application under section 633 or 634 (objection to variation of class rights) forward a copy of the order to the registrar.
@ref s 635(1) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: in time (src:8491)
GIVEN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634` IS A DATE
      `the date the company forwarded a copy of the order to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(1) the company forwarded a copy of the order to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company forwarded a copy of the order to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a copy of the order given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 635(1) the last day for the copy of the order` `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must within 15 days after the making of an order by the court on an application under section 633 or 634 (objection to variation of class rights) forward a copy of the order to the registrar"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 635(1) the last day for the copy of the order` `the date the court made an order on an application under section 633 or 634`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must within 15 days after the making of an order by the court on an application under section 633 or 634 (objection to variation of class rights) forward a copy of the order to the registrar" (the period of 15 days has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 15 days has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

-- src:8491 | (1) The company must within 15 days after the making of an order by the court on an application under section 633 or 634 (objection to variation of class rights) forward a copy of the order to the registrar.
@ref s 635(1) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: the duty (src:8491)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 635(1) the company's duty to forward a copy of the order to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` Company Registrar "forward a copy of the order to the registrar"
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "a copy of the order was not forwarded to the registrar within 15 days after the court made it"


-- src:8492 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:8493 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8494 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 635(2) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: default (src:8492-8494)
GIVEN requirements IS A LIST OF (MAYBE BOOLEAN)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(2) default is made in complying with this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST FALSE) requirements
        THEN JUST TRUE -- a requirement of the section is not met
        IF all (GIVEN r YIELD r EQUALS JUST TRUE) requirements
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section" (every requirement of the section is met)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a requirement is not yet known to be met or not met


-- src:8492 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:8493 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8494 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 635(2) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: the company (src:8492-8494)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(2)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `default is made in complying with this section`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether default is made is not yet known

-- src:8492 | (2) If default is made in complying with this section an offence is committed by—
-- src:8493 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8494 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 635(2) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: the officer (src:8492-8494)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with this section` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 635(2)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If default is made in complying with this section, an offence is committed by"
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "every officer of the company who is in default" (the officer is not in default, as s 1121 answers)
        IF `default is made in complying with this section` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether default is made, or whether the officer is in default (s 1121, coa24), is not known


-- src:8495 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 635(3) Copy of court order to be forwarded to the registrar: the penalty (src:8495)
GIVEN `the person is guilty of an offence under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 635(3) the penalty for a person guilty of an offence under this section` MEANS
    IF `the person is guilty of an offence under this section`
    THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
            `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
            `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
            `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 1)
            `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 3 0.1)
            `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the liability is that of "A person guilty of an offence under this section"


§§ `s 636 Notice of name or other designation of class of shares`

-- src:8498 | (1) Where a company assigns a name or other designation, or a new name or other designation, to any class or description of its shares, it must within one month from doing so deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation so assigned.
@ref s 636(1) Notice of name or other designation of class of shares (src:8498)
GIVEN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 636(1) the last day for the notice` MEANS `add months` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` 1

GIVEN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 636(1) the number of days allowed for the notice` MEANS
    (Day (`s 636(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`)) MINUS (Day `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`)

-- src:8498 | (1) Where a company assigns a name or other designation, or a new name or other designation, to any class or description of its shares, it must within one month from doing so deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation so assigned.
@ref s 636(1) Notice of name or other designation of class of shares: in time (src:8498)
GIVEN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares` IS A DATE
      `the date the company delivered the notice to the registrar, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date being asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 636(1) the company delivered the notice to the registrar in time` MEANS
    `the answer on the dates`
    WHERE
        `the answer on the dates` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the company delivered the notice to the registrar, if it has`
            WHEN JUST given THEN
                BRANCH
                    IF given LESS THAN `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`
                    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period runs "after" the event and a notice given before it is not within the period
                    IF given AT MOST `s 636(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`
                    THEN JUST TRUE
                    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month from doing so deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation so assigned"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the date being asked about` GREATER THAN `s 636(1) the last day for the notice` `the date the company assigned a name or other designation to a class or description of its shares`
                THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it must within one month from doing so deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation so assigned" (the period of 1 month has ended and nothing was given)
                ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the period of 1 month has not ended, so the text does not yet say whether the duty is met

-- src:8498 | (1) Where a company assigns a name or other designation, or a new name or other designation, to any class or description of its shares, it must within one month from doing so deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation so assigned.
@ref s 636(1) Notice of name or other designation of class of shares: the duty (src:8498)
GIVEN `the number of days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Action of a party`
`s 636(1) the company's duty to deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation assigned to the class of shares` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `Action of a party` Company Registrar "deliver to the registrar a notice giving particulars of the name or designation assigned to the class of shares"
    WITHIN `the number of days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the notice was not delivered within one month from assigning the name or designation"


